                <zone h='57812' id='37' type-v2='text' w='10395' x='89019' y='41146'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='8'>Key finding: Low comorbidity burden hospitals ($14,493) show higher payments </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='8'>per discharge than high burden hospitals ($12,045) — a $2,448 gap. This </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='8'>counterintuitive finding reflects specialty hospital influence, where facilities </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='8'>with lower recorded comorbidity indices receive higher Medicare payments due to </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='8'>specialized reimbursement structures. 1,057 hospitals fall in the high burden tier.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='8'>Data note: Comorbidity index = sum of 14 physical condition prevalences. </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='8'>Tiers defined by 33rd and 66th percentile thresholds of the comorbidity index.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
